  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array BBB consisting of non-negative integers, let g(B,x)g(B, x)g(B,x) denote the maximum possible MEX†{MEX}^\\dagMEX† of the array BBB we can obtain, by appending xxx integers to BBB.\n\nFor example, g([1,2,4],1)=3g([1, 2, 4], 1) = 3g([1,2,4],1)=3 as we can obtain the array [1,2,4,0][1, 2, 4, 0][1,2,4,0] by appending 000 which results in MEX=3MEX = 3MEX=3.\n\nIt can be shown that there exists a non-negative integer CCC such that g(B,x+1)−g(B,x)=1g(B, x + 1) - g(B, x) = 1g(B,x+1)−g(B,x)=1 for all x≥Cx \\ge Cx≥C. We define f(B)f(B)f(B) as the **minimum** such CCC.\n\nGiven an array AAA of size NNN, find ∑L=1N∑R=LNf(A[L,R])\\displaystyle{\\sum_{L = 1}^{N}\\sum_{R = L}^{N} f(A[L,R])}L=1∑N​R=L∑N​f(A[L,R]), where A[L,R]A[L, R]A[L,R] represents the subarray [AL,AL+1,…,AR][A_L, A_{L+1}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,…,AR​].\n\n†MEX{ }^\\dag MEX†MEX is the minimum excluded element, i.e., the minimum non-negative integer that does not appear in the array. For example, the MEXMEXMEX of [2,0,1,4][2, 0, 1, 4][2,0,1,4] is 333 and the MEXMEXMEX of [1][1][1] is 000.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN - the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the required sum.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1041 \\le T \\le 2 \\cdot 10^41≤T≤2⋅104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai&lt;N0 \\le A_i \\lt N0≤Ai​&lt;N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
