      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n2\n1 0\n3\n1 1 2\n6\n1 4 0 1 3 0\n1\n0",
        "output": "1\n7\n32\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111 : It can be shown that f([0])=0f([0]) = 0f([0])=0, f([1])=1f([1]) = 1f([1])=1, f([0,1])=0f([0, 1]) = 0f([0,1])=0. Thus, the sum is 111.\nTest case 222 :\n\nf([1])=1f([1]) = 1f([1])=1. The count of [1][1][1] in the given array is 222.\nf([2])=2f([2]) = 2f([2])=2\nf([1,1])=1f([1,1]) = 1f([1,1])=1\nf([1,2])=1f([1,2]) = 1f([1,2])=1\nf([1,1,2])=1f([1, 1, 2]) = 1f([1,1,2])=1 because g([1,1,2],0)=0g([1, 1, 2], 0) = 0g([1,1,2],0)=0, g([1,1,2],1)=3g([1, 1, 2], 1) = 3g([1,1,2],1)=3, g([1,1,2],2)=4g([1, 1, 2], 2) = 4g([1,1,2],2)=4, g([1,1,2],3)=5g([1, 1, 2], 3) = 5g([1,1,2],3)=5, and it can be verified that for all x≥1x \\ge 1x≥1, g([1,1,2],x+1)−g([1,1,2],x)=1g([1, 1, 2], x + 1) - g([1, 1, 2], x) = 1g([1,1,2],x+1)−g([1,1,2],x)=1 holds.\n\nThus, the required sum is 1⋅2+2+1+1+1=71\\cdot 2+2+1+1+1 = 71⋅2+2+1+1+1=7."
